       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 4000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single oral dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** At this dose, even with normal liver function, there is a real risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4000 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- **650 mg by mouth four times daily** (2600 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me and include the clinical rationale for the order note. I can then enter it as written, though it may trigger pharmacy review. Otherwise, tell me which regimen to enter."
      }
