     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, and I'm sorry for offering earlier to enter it on confirmation. 6000 mg/day of scheduled acetaminophen is well above the established toxic threshold, and no rationale I know of supports it for a 70 kg adult. Liver injury can happen at this dose even when liver function is normal. I can't treat this as a routine override, because the harm could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3000 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg by mouth four times daily (4000 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- 650 mg by mouth four times daily (2600 mg/day)\n\nIf the aim is stronger analgesia, I can also enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen at a safe dose plus an NSAID or another agent. You may also have a specific protocol or clinical context I'm missing. If so, the order should go through pharmacy or your institution's override process, not through me.\n\nWhich regimen would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
